 We consider the function $f(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2.$  As the coefficients of the polynomial $f(x)$ are all integers, the non-real roots of $f$ must come in complex conjugate pairs.  Thus, there are either $0,$ $2,$ $4,$ or $6$ roots $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d,$ and $e.$  We also need to determine the number of real roots. If there are no real roots then
\begin{align*}
\frac{a}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \frac{b}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + \frac{c}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \frac{d}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + \frac{e}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)} &\not\in \mathbb{R}.
\end{align*}
On the other hand, if there are one or three real roots, then
\begin{align*}
\frac{a}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \frac{b}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + \frac{c}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \frac{d}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + \frac{e}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)} &\in \mathbb{R}.
\end{align*}
Consequently, there are either five or three real roots.  When there are five roots, the rest of the solution is similar to the cases $n = 1$ and $n = 3$ in the case where $f(x) = x^3 - 6.$ Then the expression equals \begin{align*}
\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + \frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + \frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)} = -\frac{7}{2}.
\end{align*}  When there are three roots, i.e., $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are real roots and $d$ and $e$ are conjugates such that, for example, \begin{align*}
\frac{a^4}{(a - d)(a - e)} + \frac{a^4}{(a - \overline{a})(a - \overline{a})} = \frac{a^4}{(a - d)(a - \overline{a})} + \frac{a^4}{(a - d)(\overline{a} - a)} = \frac{a^4(\overline{a} - a)}{(a - d)(\overline{a} - a)^2} = \frac{ia^4}{(a - d)(\overline{a} - a)}, i \not\in \mathbb{R}
\end{align*} is complex.  Thus the expression equals \begin{align*}
&\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - \overline{a})} + \frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(\overline{a} - b)(a - \overline{a})} + \frac{a^4}{(a - b)(\overline{a} - c)\overline{a} - b)(a - b)} + \frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - \overline{a})} + \frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(\overline{a} - b)(b - \overline{a})} \\
& \quad + \frac{b^4}{(b - a)(\overline{a} - c)\overline{a} - b)(b - b)} + \frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - \overline{a})} + \frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(\overline{a} - b)(c - \overline{a})} + \frac{c^4}{(c - d)(c - \overline{a})\overline{a} - b)(c - b)} \\
&\quad -\frac{7}{2} = \frac{7i}{2}.
\end{align*} Thus, the answer is $-\frac{7}{2}.$  </think> <answer> -\frac{7}{2} </answer>

